}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Sashimi Cat''' at Level 10.

Evolves into '''Xmas Pudding Cat''' when obtained from the [[Reindeer Fish Awakens!]] (may be dropped on the first stage but guaranteed on the second stage) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Reindeer Fish Cat is a variant of [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Fish Cat]] with the [[:Category:Cats with Money Up ability|Money Up]] ability. As a variant of Fish Cat, this unit heavily underperforms as an attacker, especially when compared to [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Fish Cat's]] raw stats and [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Fish Cat's]] raw stat boost gained from plus levels. As an attacker, he's only useful for beginners, whereas for mid to late game players, his true value lies in the [[Cat Combo]]s he's in, primarily being used in the combos [[Bento Special (Combo)|Bento Special]], [[Reindeer's Gift (Combo)|Reindeer's Gift]] or [[Fresh Catch (Combo)|Fresh Catch]].

==='''True Form'''===
Xmas Pudding Cat gains higher health, area attack, and faster attack speed. Sadly, this unit still has the same weaknesses, mainly low range. It is more convenient to use other Bounty cats like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev/Bullet Train Cat]], [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] due to both having much higher stats. His only redemption he has is having Area Attack and can be used in {{4c}} stages due to his better stats than an untalented [[Thief Cat (Rare Cat)|Goemon Cat]]. However, If Goemon Cat is talented with Strengthen or Speed or has a lot of +levels and Catseyes are invested, then there is no reason to use Xmas Pudding Cat over Goemon Cat. In [[Legend Stages|Uncanny Legends]], due to Xmas Pudding Cat's low stats, this unit is unusable.

{{Job|Classification = Melee & Combo Slave}}

