==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Reindeer Fish Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Reindeer Fish Cat
The Cats tried making the Fish Cat cuter.
This one carries the gifts you dream of.
More money earned when defeating an enemy.</pre>
<pre>Sashimi Cat
The Cats tried making the Fish Cat look tastier.
Earned stars in hospitality for its sacrifice.
More money earned when defeating an enemy.</pre>
<pre>Xmas Pudding Cat
This unit built for fighting has been re-
engineered to delight sweet tooths. Area
attacks get extra money after defeating.</pre>
**According to Sashimi Cat's original description, Fish Cat was the only Cat Unit with [[wikipedia:Service star|service stars]].
*The Normal Form of this cat is a reference to Santa Claus.
*The Fish Cat in the Evolved Form is most likely cooked, as it is slightly described in its entry. It is laying down on a basket and the two cats in front are holding forks. Most likely a reference to traditional Christmas meals.
**Also, [[Offering to the Gods (Combo)|one of this Unit's combos]] implies that Fish Cat was offered to as a sacrifice to [[Shining Amaterasu (Uber Rare Cat)|Shining Amaterasu]].
*According to Sashimi Cat's description, Fish Cat is the only Cat Unit with [[wikipedia:Service star|service stars]].
*Unlike other variants of Fish Cat, this unit lacks the [[Strong Against|Strong]] ability.
*The [[Catnip Challenges|Missions]] refer to this Cat as 'Reindeer Cat' instead of 'Reindeer Fish Cat'.
*Reindeer Fish Cat's Upgrade Costs are almost exactly the same as a typical Rare Cat, except for Levels 9, 19, 29, 39, and 49, which all cost slightly more XP.

